WEBVTT

00:00.425 --> 00:02.631
- [Voiceover] Let's
say that we had a cube,

00:02.631 --> 00:04.744
let me draw the cube here,

00:04.744 --> 00:07.971
So we have a cube, and we know

00:07.971 --> 00:12.475
that the volume of this cube is equal to

00:12.475 --> 00:17.119
512 cubic centimeters.

00:17.119 --> 00:19.488
So my question to you is, what are

00:19.488 --> 00:21.856
the dimensions of this cube?

00:21.856 --> 00:25.176
So what is this length gonna be?

00:25.176 --> 00:27.475
What is this, I guess you could say depth,

00:27.475 --> 00:29.193
and what is this height going to be?

00:29.193 --> 00:31.097
And, we know it's a cube, so these are

00:31.097 --> 00:33.071
all going to be equal.

00:33.071 --> 00:35.091
And so like always, encourage
you to pause the video

00:35.091 --> 00:37.602
and try to figure it out.

00:37.602 --> 00:40.826
Well let's call this length x.

00:40.826 --> 00:42.614
If that's x then this is going to be x,

00:42.614 --> 00:44.518
and then this is x as well.

00:44.518 --> 00:47.954
So if the volume is 512 cubic centimeters,

00:47.954 --> 00:50.531
that means that

00:50.531 --> 00:54.268
x times x times x

00:54.268 --> 00:57.078
is going to be equal to 512.

00:57.078 --> 00:59.370
Is going to be equal to 512,

00:59.370 --> 01:01.320
or we could say that x to the third power

01:01.320 --> 01:03.178
is equal to 512,

01:03.178 --> 01:04.815
or we could say that x is equal

01:04.815 --> 01:09.325
to the cube root of 512.

01:09.325 --> 01:11.456
So what's the cube root of 512?

01:11.456 --> 01:13.808
And the easiest way I can
think about doing this,

01:13.808 --> 01:15.038
if I don't have a calculator,

01:15.038 --> 01:18.777
is to just try to do a prime
factorization of this by hand.

01:18.777 --> 01:20.819
So that's what I'm going to attempt to do.

01:20.819 --> 01:23.094
So let's see, does two go into 512?

01:23.094 --> 01:25.811
Sure, 512s even, so this is going to be

01:25.811 --> 01:30.017
two times, let's see, 256, yeah,

01:30.017 --> 01:33.569
two times 256.

01:33.569 --> 01:36.796
256 that's also divisible by two.

01:36.796 --> 01:39.351
That's two times 128,

01:39.351 --> 01:40.817
which is also divisible by two,

01:40.817 --> 01:44.295
that's two time 64,

01:44.295 --> 01:45.664
which is also divisible by two.

01:45.664 --> 01:47.917
That's two times 32,

01:47.917 --> 01:50.006
let's see, I can keep going,

01:50.006 --> 01:51.957
that's two times 16.

01:51.957 --> 01:55.625
Which is two times eight,

01:55.625 --> 01:57.274
which is two times four,

01:57.274 --> 01:59.782
which is two times two.

01:59.782 --> 02:01.477
So 512 that's the same thing as

02:01.477 --> 02:03.148
two to the, let's see you have,

02:03.148 --> 02:05.284
one, two, three, four, five, six,

02:05.284 --> 02:07.049
seven, eight, nine.

02:07.049 --> 02:08.930
That's two to the ninth power.

02:08.930 --> 02:09.812
But what we care about is

02:09.812 --> 02:13.527
what times itself times itself is equal,

02:13.527 --> 02:15.176
what number, if I have three of 'em

02:15.176 --> 02:18.380
and I multiply 'em
together, get us to 512?

02:18.380 --> 02:19.796
And to think about that, we could say,

02:19.796 --> 02:21.956
"Look, I have nine numbers here.

02:21.956 --> 02:23.953
"So let me divide into three groups."

02:23.953 --> 02:26.530
So if this is one group,

02:26.530 --> 02:29.502
and this is the next group,

02:29.502 --> 02:31.336
and then this is the next group

02:31.336 --> 02:33.635
right over here,

02:33.635 --> 02:35.887
we could say that 512 is the same thing as

02:35.887 --> 02:38.139
two times two times two, which is eight,

02:38.139 --> 02:40.647
times two times two times
two, which is eight,

02:40.647 --> 02:43.294
times two times two times two.

02:43.294 --> 02:47.636
So 512 is the same thing as
eight to the third power.

02:47.636 --> 02:50.090
So we could say, that,

02:50.090 --> 02:52.184
x, I'll do it over here,

02:52.184 --> 02:55.342
x is equal to the cube root of,

02:55.342 --> 02:57.478
instead of writing 512,

02:57.478 --> 02:58.964
instead of writing 512,

02:58.964 --> 03:01.379
I could write eight to the third power.

03:01.379 --> 03:03.770
Now, what's the cube root of
something to the third power?

03:03.770 --> 03:05.558
Well, it's just gonna be this something.

03:05.558 --> 03:09.668
So x, x is going to be equal to eight.

03:09.668 --> 03:12.826
So if the volume here is
512 cubic centimeters,

03:12.826 --> 03:15.705
each dimension is going
to be eight centimeters.

03:15.705 --> 03:19.327
So x is equal to eight centimeters.

03:19.327 --> 03:20.999
This is equal to eight centimeters.

03:20.999 --> 03:22.438
I'm just writing the units now.

03:22.438 --> 03:24.203
This is equal to eight centimeters,

03:24.203 --> 03:25.341
and we're done.

03:25.341 --> 03:26.571
But, if you didn't know offhand

03:26.571 --> 03:28.220
that eight to the third power is 512,

03:28.220 --> 03:31.354
this is a reasonable way of
coming to that conclusion.

03:31.354 --> 03:33.296
Anyway, hopefully that helped.
